<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
	Chapters and bookmarks, in the Video OSD's look (0.28.1): the player top bar (heading and count on the left, Skippy's
	next episode, clock box, weather box), a dark scrim at the bottom with the three buttons and the playing time, then
	a strip of 16:9 thumbs (chapters + bookmarks; Kodi lists both, label = name, label2 = time). Opened from the OSD
	chapters button (70044) and with Down from the OSD buttons.

	Thumbs: Kodi's own (a frame it extracts per chapter, often never arriving on large files, or a bookmark's picture)
	drawn over the cell of the Trickplay sprites next to the video, which the helper crops when this opens
	(RunScript(script.aeon.helper,chapthumbs), Window(Home).Property(aeon.chap.prefix)). So the Trickplay picture shows
	wherever Kodi has none.

	Id contract (Estuary Omega VideoOSDBookmarks.xml / GUIDialogVideoBookmarks.cpp): 2 add bookmark
	(default, always), 3 clear bookmarks, 4 add episode bookmark (Kodi enables it for episodes),
	11 thumbs panel (OK jumps to the chapter/bookmark). 9001 = button row.
	Focus map: buttons Left/Right, Down -> thumbs, Up from thumbs -> buttons. Back closes.
-->
<window>
	<defaultcontrol always="true">2</defaultcontrol>
	<onload>RunScript(script.aeon.helper,chapthumbs)</onload>
	<!-- opened with Down from the player: land on the chapter thumbnails, Up reaches the buttons -->
	<onload condition="$EXP[OSD_HasChapters]">AlarmClock(aeonchap,SetFocus(11),00:00,silent)</onload>
	<include>Anim_OSDSlideUp</include>
	<controls>
		<include condition="Skin.HasSetting(aeon.fglass)">FG_Bookmarks</include>
		<include condition="!Skin.HasSetting(aeon.fglass)">OSD_Bookmarks_Classic</include>
	</controls>
</window>
